      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\n(1 comment)\n\nExperimental feature testing in progress, please pay attention to the comments\n\nThe change is functionally safe: lockdep_off()/lockdep_on() only gate the runtime lock validator, not actual lock acquisition, so removing the balanced pairs cannot alter locking behavior on production kernels and simply lets lockdep validate the mount and key-link paths as intended. One small cleanup note left inline; the same leftover blank line also appears before `return rc;` in lustre_fill_super() and lustre_tgt_fill_super().",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
