        "subject": "LU-20422 misc: enable lockdep unconditionally",
        "message": "LU-20422 misc: enable lockdep unconditionally\n\nLustre's locking is not so special as to require disabling\nlockdep via lockdep_on() / lockdep_off(). Remove all callers\nof these functions. Lustre only has a handful of lockdep errors.\nAnd it has lockdep error regardless of whether these callers\nare present. Remove them - developers should fix lockdeps errors\nrather than ignore them.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Timothy Day <timday@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I3b5d41db42829009c943085b6cc277dc2d6d99b2\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66821\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: James Simmons <jsimmons@infradead.org>\nReviewed-by: Shaun Tancheff <shaun.tancheff@hpe.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\n"
      },
